    "readout_text": "To determine how many square centimeters of paper Jackson can cover with paint, we need to calculate the area of the paint strip he can create and then convert that area from square millimeters to square centimeters.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Convert the length to millimeters\n\nJackson's paintbrush makes a strip that is **25 meters long**. Since 1 meter = 1000 millimeters:\n\n$$\n25 \\text{ meters} = 25 \\times 1000 = 25,000 \\text{ millimeters}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the area in square millimeters\n\nThe width of the strip is **6.5 millimeters**, and the length is **25,000 millimeters**. The area of the strip is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area} = \\text{width} \\times \\text{length} = 6.5 \\times 25,000 = 162,500 \\text{ square millimeters}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Convert square millimeters to square centimeters\n\nWe know that:\n\n$$\n1 \\text{ cm} = 10 \\text{ mm} \\Rightarrow 1 \\text{ cm}^2 = 100 \\text{ mm}^2\n$$\n\nSo, to convert square millimeters to square centimeters:\n\n$$\n162,500 \\text{ mm}^2 \\div 100 = 1,625 \\text{ cm}^2\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{1625}\n$$\n\nJackson could cover **1,625 square centimeters** of paper with paint.",
